{
  "NotebookModel": "my-nbfc",
  "Author": "Isma",
  "Comment": "PATH: /usr/share/nbfc/configs/. MinSpeed 12% at first step prevents the yoyo effect (fan oscillating 0<->12% around 48-50C). DownThreshold=0 on step 0 ensures the fan never fully stops once spun up. The four lowest steps' *speeds* were lowered (12/16/20/24 -> 12/12/15/18) rather than their thresholds: raising a threshold was measured to buy nothing (the loop re-equilibrates at the same duty, just hotter), while lowering the duty is what actually changes the rpm. The steps from 74C up are untouched, so the heavy-load envelope is unchanged. On battery the SMU caps Tctl at 65C regardless, so the extra few degrees are bounded by the firmware, not by this curve.",
